{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FULL UNIT TIER FOUND TWO REAL DEFECTS THAT LINT + TYPECHECK + TARGETED TESTS ALL MISSED.\nResult was 2 failed / 14,995 passed / 53 skipped in 49m. Both failures mine; both now fixed at the\nright layer and folded into the right commits.\n\n 1. tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py::test_the_unrelated_o_excl_uses_survive —\n    'an unrelated O_EXCL use moved in _store/fsutil.py'. That test pins fsutil.py to EXACTLY ONE\n    occurrence of the literal O_EXCL; the audit docstring added for b0ac introduced a second.\n    Fixed by REWORDING my prose ('its own exclusively-created name') rather than bumping the\n    expected count — the count IS the test's precision, and relaxing an unrelated guard to\n    accommodate my own docstring would be the wrong trade. Belongs to 2505; amended there.\n\n 2. tests/unit/test_nested_pytest_uniqueness.py::test_the_launch_appears_only_in_the_helper —\n    'nested pytest is launched outside tests/_nested_pytest.py'. MY OWN isolation-guard oracle\n    spawned pytest --collect-only directly. The repo has exactly one sanctioned nested-pytest\n    launcher, and an escape marker exists — but taking the escape hatch in the very change that\n    ADDS an isolation guard would be poor form, so I routed the call through\n    run_nested_pytest(tmp_path, ..., env=subprocess_env(), timeout=1800), which owns the child's\n    --basetemp. Belongs to 2506; amended there. 27/27 guard tests still pass.\n    Note the shape: a grep-based guard could not police this (Black splits argv one element per\n    line so '-m','pytest' never appear adjacently), which is why that test is a structural AST scan\n    over any list/tuple literal.\n\nFINAL STACK, all six Change-Ids preserved across five rounds of amend+rebase:\n 6ecba4218c86 2503 parity  -> e456f39d625c 2504 mirrors -> 69dab8d4de07 2505 atomic\n -> 9fc16d68bd07 2506 guard -> f5ee32d4a9cf 2507 measurement -> 356ca2c38ebc ratchet (new)\nDefinitive full tier running on a stable tree with no concurrent git operations."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788327762640808001,"uuid":"a4508675-6484-4de9-b88c-765c44827388"}